quran[6]{c,v,t}:
  5,65,"But had the People of the Book only believed and remained God-conscious, We would have surely acquitted them of their misdeeds and admitted them to the Gardens of bliss."
  5,66,"Had they observed (the commandments of) the Torah and the Injil (the Gospel) and whatever was revealed to them from their Lord, they would surely have received nourishment from above them and from beneath their feet. There is a moderate (and upright) community among them, but what most of them are doing is evil."
  5,67,"Esteemed Messenger! Convey everything that has been revealed to you from your Lord. And if you do not, then you have not delivered His Message. Allah shall protect you from the people. Indeed, Allah does not guide the disbelieving people."
  5,68,"Say: ‘O People of the Book, you do not stand on anything unless you observe (the commandments of) the Torah and the Injil (the Gospel) and whatever has been revealed to you from your Lord.’ And what has been revealed to you from your Lord will surely increase many of them in rebellion and disbelief. So do not worry about the disbelieving people."
  5,69,"Indeed, the believers, the Jews, the Sabaeans, and the Christians, whoever (truly) believes in Allah and the Last Day and acts righteously, there shall be no fear on them, nor shall they grieve."
  5,70,"Surely, We took a pledge from the Children of Israel and sent messengers to them. Whenever a messenger brought them what their souls did not desire, they would accuse some of lying, and some they would slay."
